The "CDDB module not installed" error means
your media software (like music players or ripping tools) can't find the necessary components to fetch album/track info from online databases, often fixed by installing specific packages (kde-config-cddb for Linux), ensuring proper setup in the app (VLC, K3b), or updating drivers/connections if it's a car system. The solution depends heavily on the software and OS, but generally involves installing missing libraries or checking settings. 

### For Linux Users (KDE/K3b)

Install the package: Open your terminal and run sudo apt install kde-config-cddb (for Ubuntu/Debian) or your distribution's equivalent to get the KCDDB module. 

sudo apt install kde-config-cddb

sudo apt install python3-musicbrainzngs


